{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_9dbbc8c4ca49db2a22138ee4bb2560af69e1b92b274005335b044f0123af46fc", "title": "Portland Exposition Building", "text": "The Portland Exposition Building, also known as The Expo, is a sports and exhibition venue (convention center) building complex in Portland, Maine. The complex includes five inter-connected buildings with 330,000 square feet of exhibition space and 10 meeting rooms. The Center is adjacent to the Hadlock Field and the Portland Ice Arena. Phish, Ani Difranco, Natalie Merchant, The Monkees, and Rusted Root have played at the venue. It has also hosted trade shows and celebrations. It has been used for the Maine Red Claws basketball team, Portland High School Bulldogs basketball games, and indoor track events. In 2007, the Expo became the home of Maine Roller Derby.", "score": 29.6256}, {"id": "hp_doc_27c78cb77a187ed280ce5b8a4b6cc7182a1716bb570cf46d9c74f0d1eb245ce5", "title": "Fitzpatrick Stadium", "text": "Fitzpatrick Stadium is a 6,300 seat multi-purpose outdoor stadium in Portland, Maine, USA. It is located between Interstate 295, Hadlock Field baseball stadium, and the Portland Exposition Building, the second oldest arena in continuous operation in the United States. It is located across the street from Deering Oaks, a public park listed on the National Register of Historic Places. Formerly known as Portland Stadium, it was renamed in 1989 to honor James J. Fitzpatrick, one of the most respected figures in Maine athletic history.", "score": 22.8683}, {"id": "hp_doc_42c84fda760a4b9d5cd6793703da72a0036b02000724c9cce37b54c9b8b7ff77", "title": "Drew Robinson &amp; Company building", "text": "Drew Robinson & Company building, also known as the Albany Light Opera Company building and Dylan's on the Terrace, is a heritage listed building located on Stirling Terrace overlooking Princess Royal Harbour in Albany in the Great Southern region of Western Australia.", "score": 11.3773}], "remaining_searches": 1}
